IMPORT prelude

-- Judges (Long Leave Payments) Act 1979 (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE RULES AND THE
-- TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C2004A02100.txt (compilation No. 6, 1
-- September 2021).
-- The Judge (or, on death, the survivors) asks: "When I stop being a Judge,
-- is a long leave payment due, how much, and to whom?"

§ `Nouns`

-- s 3 Judge.
DECLARE `Judicial office` IS ONE OF
    `a Judge of a federal court other than the High Court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court (Division 2)`
    `a person with the same status as such a Judge by virtue of an Act`
    `a Judge of the ACT Supreme Court immediately before the 1992 transfer`
    `a Justice of the High Court`
    `a Judge of the Federal Circuit and Family Court (Division 2) only`

-- How I cease to be a Judge (s 3 retirement, s 4, s 7).
DECLARE `Ceasing` IS ONE OF
    `I resign or my term ends`
    `I reach the age at which I must cease to hold office`
    `I am removed under section 72 of the Constitution or a like provision`
    `I die`

-- s 5: to whom the amount is paid.
DECLARE `Recipient` IS ONE OF
    `me`
    `my surviving spouse or de facto partner`
    `my dependants`
    `my legal personal representative`
    `no one`

DECLARE `Judge case` HAS
    `my office`                                             IS A `Judicial office`
    `how I cease`                                           IS A `Ceasing`
    -- s 3A
    `a new appointment as a Judge takes effect immediately` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 4(3): service as a Judge (for s 6 of the Judges' Pensions Act 1968), in years
    `my years of service as a Judge`                        IS A NUMBER
    -- s 4(3): qualifying service, excluding periods of long leave taken or paid in lieu, in years
    `my years of qualifying service`                        IS A NUMBER
    -- s 3 judicial salary: the annual salary immediately before ceasing
    `my annual salary immediately before`                   IS A NUMBER
    -- s 4(2B)(b)
    `the Attorney-General certifies permanent disability or infirmity` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 7
    `the Governor-General directs payment`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 5(2)
    `I leave a surviving spouse or de facto partner`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `I leave dependants`                                    IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Long leave position` HAS
    `weeks of judicial salary payable`                      IS A NUMBER
    `the amount payable`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `it is payable to`                                      IS A `Recipient`

§ `Rules`

-- s 3 Judge; s 3B: also holding a Division 2 office does not matter.
@ref ss 3, 3B
GIVEN c IS A `Judge case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am a Judge for this Act` c IF
        c's `my office` EQUALS `a Judge of a federal court other than the High Court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court (Division 2)`
    OR  c's `my office` EQUALS `a person with the same status as such a Judge by virtue of an Act`
    OR  c's `my office` EQUALS `a Judge of the ACT Supreme Court immediately before the 1992 transfer`

-- s 3 retirement: ceasing otherwise than by death; s 3A: not where a new
-- appointment takes effect immediately after.
@ref ss 3, 3A
GIVEN c IS A `Judge case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I retire` c IF
        NOT (c's `how I cease` EQUALS `I die`)
    AND NOT (c's `a new appointment as a Judge takes effect immediately`)

GIVEN c IS A `Judge case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I die in office` c IF c's `how I cease` EQUALS `I die`

-- s 7: no amount on removal, unless the Governor-General directs.
@ref s 7
GIVEN c IS A `Judge case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `removal bars payment` c IF
        c's `how I cease` EQUALS `I am removed under section 72 of the Constitution or a like provision`
    AND NOT (c's `the Governor-General directs payment`)

-- s 4(1): retirement after at least 10 years' service, or death.
@ref s 4(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Judge case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4(1) applies to` c IF
        (`I retire` c AND c's `my years of service as a Judge` AT LEAST 10)
    OR  `I die in office` c

-- s 4(2A): ceasing on attaining the age, with at least 6 years' service.
-- s 4(2B): retirement certified as due to permanent disability or infirmity.
@ref s 4(2A)-(2B)
GIVEN c IS A `Judge case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4(2A) or (2B) applies to` c IF
        NOT (`section 4(1) applies to` c)
    AND `I retire` c
    AND (   (    c's `how I cease` EQUALS `I reach the age at which I must cease to hold office`
             AND c's `my years of service as a Judge` AT LEAST 6)
         OR c's `the Attorney-General certifies permanent disability or infirmity`)

-- s 4(2), (2C): 5.2 weeks for each completed year of qualifying service; under
-- s 4(1), no more than 52 weeks.
@ref s 4(2), (2C)
GIVEN c IS A `Judge case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weeks payable for` c MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`I am a Judge for this Act` c)) OR `removal bars payment` c
            THEN 0
        IF `section 4(1) applies to` c
            THEN `the smaller of` 52 `and` (`the 5.2 weeks rate for` c)
        IF `section 4(2A) or (2B) applies to` c
            THEN `the 5.2 weeks rate for` c
        OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN c IS A `Judge case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 5.2 weeks rate for` c MEANS
    52 TIMES (FLOOR (c's `my years of qualifying service`)) DIVIDED BY 10

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` a `and` b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

-- s 3 judicial salary: a weekly rate of one fifty-second of the annual salary.
@ref ss 3, 4(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Judge case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount payable for` c MEANS
    `the weeks payable for` c TIMES c's `my annual salary immediately before` DIVIDED BY 52

-- s 5(1)-(2). An amount payable under s 4 has a payee even when it is nil
-- (changed after the independent pass).
@ref s 5(1)-(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Judge case`
GIVETH A `Recipient`
`the recipient for` c MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`I am a Judge for this Act` c)) OR `removal bars payment` c OR NOT (`section 4(1) applies to` c OR `section 4(2A) or (2B) applies to` c)
            THEN `no one`
        IF NOT (`I die in office` c)
            THEN `me`
        IF c's `I leave a surviving spouse or de facto partner`
            THEN `my surviving spouse or de facto partner`
        IF c's `I leave dependants`
            THEN `my dependants`
        OTHERWISE `my legal personal representative`

@ref ss 3-5, 7
@export default The long leave payment under the Judges (Long Leave Payments) Act 1979 (Cth) when a federal Judge ceases to hold office: on retirement after at least 10 years' service, or on death, judicial salary for 5.2 weeks per completed year of qualifying service, at most 52 weeks (s 4(1)-(2)); on ceasing at the compulsory age after at least 6 years, or retirement certified as due to permanent disability, 5.2 weeks per completed year without the cap (s 4(2A)-(2C)); nothing on immediate reappointment (s 3A) or on removal unless the Governor-General directs (s 7); paid to the Judge, or on death to the surviving spouse or de facto partner, else the dependants, else the legal personal representative (s 5). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Judge case`  @desc My office, how I cease to hold it, my service and qualifying service in years, my salary, and any certificate, direction or survivors
GIVETH A `Long leave position`
`the long leave position for` c MEANS
    `Long leave position` OF `the weeks payable for` c, `the amount payable for` c, `the recipient for` c
